Subject: [PATCH] flac: gate FLAC__SYS_LINUX on the os field, not the vendor

flac decides it is on Linux by matching $host against *-pc-linux-gnu, so any
triple with a vendor other than pc silently loses FLAC__SYS_LINUX and builds
as though the platform were unknown. Spike 5 walked all 2893 el8 source
packages looking for exactly this shape and flac is the only live instance;
the eighteen other literal matches are comments and test fixtures.

The fix is the one upstream eventually made: match the os field, which is
what the test meant all along. *-*-linux-gnu* covers *-pc-linux-gnu, so no
existing build changes.

Only configure.ac is patched. flac's el8 spec runs ./autogen.sh at %prep, so
the generated configure carrying the same line is rebuilt from this one; a
patch to it would be applied and then discarded, which reads as a second fix
and is not one.

Against flac-1.3.2-11.el8, sha256
912d166b2b1b9655047b28345288dff26933964f39261d136b82bc12b00fc73d on the
source rpm. The triple this exists to accommodate is in
doc/target-definition.md.

--- a/configure.ac
+++ b/configure.ac
@@ -186,7 +186,7 @@
 AM_CONDITIONAL(OS_IS_WINDOWS, test "x$os_is_windows" = xyes)
 
 case "$host" in
-	*-pc-linux-gnu)
+	*-*-linux-gnu*)
 		sys_linux=true
 		AC_DEFINE(FLAC__SYS_LINUX)
 		AH_TEMPLATE(FLAC__SYS_LINUX, [define if building for Linux])
